      "writtenOn": "2020-11-13T21:46:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the iterator being returned will capture a reference to `merkle_tree`, you need to tie the lifetime of the returned iterator to the lifetime of the `merkle_tree` you can do that by adding a `+ \u0027a` which is the lifetime annotation on `merkle_tree`.\n\n`Result\u003cimpl Iterator\u003cItem \u003d Result\u003c([u8; 4096], usize), FsverityError\u003e\u003e + \u0027a, FsverityError\u003e`\n\nWithout this extra annotation any references in the returned value would need to be \u0027static to be safe otherwise the reference might be able to outlive what is being referenced.",
